@cc [owner:spolu,label:testing;architecture] workload-through-grpc
Workloads MUST exercise the running server through gRPC only, without server resources, direct FDB
access, or mocks. Expected contents, namespace, metadata, and versions MUST be computed independently
from the operations issued. Unexpected errors or mismatches MUST fail the process with context.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:testing;security] workload-isolated-fixtures
Each run MUST create its own uniquely named tenants and mutate only objects it creates. Bearer keys
MUST NOT be logged. Mutations with unknown outcomes MUST NOT be automatically replayed. Random
workloads MUST report their seed, worker, and step on failure so the operation sequence is reproducible.
